    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In the heart of the hilltop village of Mougins, on Place du Commandant Lamy, La Place de Mougins is a fine-dining restaurant recognised by the Michelin Guide (selection, two place settings) and Gault&Millau, run by chef Denis Fétisson. A signature tasting menu is offered at €130.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>A notably rare detail worth flagging: the restaurant's own website carries a page titled "Nos amis les chiens" ("Our canine friends"), explicitly confirming that dogs (like groups and people with reduced mobility) are welcome. This is an official statement from the establishment itself, a solid level of confirmation.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: this is a fine-dining table, so book ahead and mention that you're bringing your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The village of Mougins, with its cobbled lanes and art galleries, is a pleasant stroll before or after the meal.</p>
